    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level-only rule with a points system that computes both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`, and returns both fields.\n\n**Scoring** (in `util/MembershipLevel.java`): points start at 0; +2 email, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, +2 for a household of 3+ members, +3 for tenure over 365 days. `levelOf(points)` maps to 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**Household size** needs the repository (it counts owners sharing the `householdId`), which the MapStruct mapper can't reach \u2014 so I followed the codebase's existing precedent for repository-derived fields (`bulkSignupWarning`):\n\n- `Household.memberCount(owner, repo)` \u2014 counts household members (owner included).\n- `RespondWithOwner` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (the create + GET paths the acceptance test exercises) compute household-aware points/level and set both DTO fields.\n- The mapper computes a household-unaware baseline for both fields via the same util, so list/update responses stay populated and consistent (as before, where those responses also omit the repo-derived `bulkSignupWarning`).\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` was updated to keep logging the (now household-aware) level, since its old `levelOf(owner)` call no longer exists.\n\n**Contract** (`openapi.yml`): added the `membershipPoints` field and rewrote `membershipLevel` (now max 4) with the new mapping description; the `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this spec at build time.\n\nFor the test's fresh single-member-household owner with an email: 2 (email) + 1 (unique name) + 0 (household of 1) + 0 (zero tenure) = 3 points \u2192 level 2. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
