    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, following the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and the code of each step. All steps run under a single `transaction` governance, so everything commits once at the end (or rolls back on any thrown escalation).\n\n## 0. Authorization (before any step)\n- `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`, else `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## 1. `ValidateNewOwner` (binds `@RequestBody`, publishes normalized DTO)\nRuns in this exact code order:\n1. **Normalize address** (side-effect, written back to request): trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. `null` \u2192 `\"\"`.\n2. **Required-field check** (validation) on the *already-normalized* values \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`. Any blank/missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) listing offending names. (Address is tested *after* normalization.)\n3. **Normalize telephone to E.164** (side-effect + validation, written back): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+`/country code, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits; national-number length must match country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n4. **Normalize email** (side-effect + validation, written back): optional (null/blank left unset); else must match the syntactic regex \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (400); lower-cased; domain checked against disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n5. **Validate postcode** (validation only): optional; when present must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known region must fall in range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown region accepts any 4-digit. Bad \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n6. **Future registration-date check** (validation): if `registrationDate` supplied and after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent is allowed.\n7. Publishes the mutated DTO as `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.\n\n## 2. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (validation)\n- If `sharesHousehold` is true, bypass. Otherwise compute household id (SHA-256 of normalized last name + `|` + trimmed postcode) and scan `findAll()`; if any existing owner shares it \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` (validation)\n- Count existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); `\u2265 50` \u2192 `OwnerCityFullException` (409).\n\n## 4. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` (validation)\n- Determine effective registration date (supplied or `now()`), roll forward to a business day, count existing owners with that `registrationDate`; `\u2265 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` (side-effect: create entity)\n- Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`; compute effective registration date (or `now()`); **roll weekend dates forward to Monday** via `BusinessDay`; set `registrationDate`. Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n## 6. `AssignCustomerCode` (side-effect, mutates entity)\n- Set `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`: region from postcode/city via `LocalityResolver`; `HASH8` = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n\n## 7. `AssignMembershipNumber` (side-effect, mutates entity)\n- Set `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`, `YY` = last two digits of registration-date year.\n\n## 8. `AssignHousehold` (side-effect, mutates entity)\n- Set `householdId` = deterministic SHA-256-based id from last name + postcode.\n\n## 9. `AssignNamesakeCount` (side-effect, mutates entity)\n- Set `namesakeCount` = number of *pre-existing* owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## 10. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (side-effect, mutates entity)\n- If `sharesHousehold` \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n- Else, among pre-existing owners with same last name (case-insensitive) + same postcode but *different* telephone, pick lowest matching id: set `possibleDuplicate` true/false and `possibleDuplicateOf` to that id (or null).\n\n## 11. `SaveOwner` (side-effect: persist)\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 assigns the generated id.\n\n## 12. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect: logging)\n- Compute membership points/level; emit an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (side-effect: response, 201)\n- Map to `OwnerDto`; set `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners share the registration day); set `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`; respond `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes worth flagging:**\n- Order matters and is deliberate: address is normalized *before* the blank check; validation (400s) precedes the 404/409/429 business checks; identity/city/daily checks all run before the entity is built or saved.\n- The three business checks (steps 2\u20134) each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and scan in memory \u2014 no side-effects, but O(n) reads.\n- Both `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` and `BuildOwner` independently apply `BusinessDay.rollForward`, so the day the limit counts against matches the day stamped on the new owner."
